# Every supply that says what it actually served, beside what it committed and how far it can
# stretch. One row per layer filing a `pm:Jagged/draw` against a stated rating.
#
# The third of the layer's three quantities
#   This is the relation that reads one. `EliminationAgainst` names all three (demand, nameplate,
#   draw) and says why the third is there: "an implementation that eliminates demand and forgets
#   the draw has silently claimed a utilisation it did not observe". The only other question
#   anything asks of a draw is whether it is absent (epistemics/absences.sqlc reads
#   `draw_absent`), so without this relation the value is read nowhere, which is the warning
#   carried out.
#
# The draw is not the demand
#   The corpus settles that rather than assuming it. The two differ at the mode more often than
#   they agree, so a reader taking one for the other is wrong more often than right; set
#   `draw_mode` beside `d_mode` from layers/demand.sqlc for the numbers. `capability` was asked
#   for 6 and served 3.
#
# A draw above the demand is not a defect
#   That is why this file reports and does not judge. `merge-pt-member/linha-partilhada` draws 10
#   where its demand reaches 8.0 at most, and the filing says why: "A produção inteira da linha...
#   a fatia do irmão está aqui dentro, e está também na declaração dele", the whole line's output,
#   of which a sibling's slice is that sibling's demand in its own filing. A rule reading "a
#   supply cannot serve more than was asked" would fire on a correct document. The bound that
#   holds is the supply's own, and it is in checks/draw_exceeds_the_supply.sqlc.
#
# A draw against no rating has no row
#   `refutation/object-storage` draws 47 with its amount filed `notApplicable`; utilisation of a
#   rating nobody stated is unanswerable, not zero. layers/absorber.sqlc states the principle.
#
# A derived draw or amount is read computed
#   The draw is composition/resolved_quantities.sqlc's, stated or computed, as layers/demand.sqlc
#   explains, and the nameplate is layers/nameplate.sqlc's, so a figure filed `derived` enters at
#   the value its fusion computes and one that cannot be computed has no row, as a typed absence has
#   none.
#
# An unmeasured capacity slack stays NULL
#   `capacity_slack` is left NULL where it is unmeasured rather than coalesced to zero. Some of
#   these layers do not know how far they can stretch, and a nameplate is not a ceiling until
#   somebody says the buffer is empty.
-- pm:Jagged/pm:draw from composition/resolved_quantities.sqlc, against layers/nameplate.sqlc and entries/slacks.sqlc's capacity slack.
SELECT dr.filing, dr.layer,
       dr.low  AS draw_low,
       dr.mode AS draw_mode,
       dr.high AS draw_high,
       dr.unit AS draw_unit,
       n.low   AS n_low,
       n.mode  AS n_mode,
       n.high  AS n_high,
       n.unit  AS n_unit,
       s.low    AS capacity_low,
       s.mode   AS capacity_slack,
       s.high   AS capacity_high,
       s.unit   AS capacity_unit,
       s.absent AS capacity_absent
FROM      (
    SELECT q.filing, q.layer, q.low, q.mode, q.high, q.unit
    FROM ( :compose(composition/resolved_quantities.sqlc) ) q
    WHERE q.quantity = 'draw'
      AND q.low IS NOT NULL
) dr
JOIN      (
    SELECT n.filing, n.layer, n.n_low AS low, n.n_mode AS mode, n.n_high AS high, n.n_unit AS unit
    FROM ( :compose(layers/nameplate.sqlc) ) n
) n ON n.filing = dr.filing AND n.layer = dr.layer
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(entries/slacks.sqlc)
) s ON s.filing = dr.filing AND s.layer = dr.layer AND s.buffer = 'capacity'
